Part 1. Dilemmas
   PDs: 7 symmetric (3 with 2R < T+S) and 300 asymmetric, both orders, round-robin and exhaustive (1228 runs): limit other than {(C,C)} in 614 runs, of which round-robin 0; first failures [(5, 3, 1, 0, (0, 1), True), (5, 3, 1, 0, (1, 0), True)]
   PD (5,3,1,0), exhaustive schedule, order (1,2): limit [(1, 0)] (player 1 raises her threshold to P, R, then T before player 2 moves)
   resolved Jacobi (Fourny rounds, one-at-a-time pass only when a round would empty the set): failures on the symmetric PDs and the TDs []
   TDs: M = 2..40, r in {1/4, 1/2, 1, 3/2, 2, 7/3, 5/2, 3, 5}, both orders, both schedules (1404 runs): limit other than {(M,M)} in 532 runs, of which round-robin 0; first failures [(3, 1, (0, 1), True, [(0, 1), (1, 1)]), (3, 1, (1, 0), True, [(1, 0), (1, 1)])]

